{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1489823-wyrm-weapon-designs","id":1489823,"title":"Wyrm Weapon Designs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-11T18:39:36-07:00","id":1489823,"title":"Wyrm Weapon Designs?","content":"Was looking at the lore, and I found myself doing some research on klaives and fetishes used by the Garou and other Fera. I noticed how different Gaia shifters had different weapon types prefered for their klaives and fetishes, such as the Get of Fenris preferring hammers, the Black Furies preferring Labrys axes, the Glass Walkers preferring firearms, and the Bastet preferring the African Hakarr.<br /> <br /> Do the servants of the Wyrm have any preferred designs for their klaives and fetish weapons? I know Baneklaives are a thing, but are there others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T09:47:57-07:00","id":1489895,"title":"","content":"BSD have a thorny whip that they produce by removing and preserving the tentacle of a particular bane. <br /> <br /> Get creative. Go wild and get disgusting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T17:22:37-07:00","id":1489979,"title":"","content":"I believe that the primary design precepts are &quot;looks like you could get tetanus just from looking at it&quot;. Also, the Bastet don't particularly care for making or using the hakarr; that was a bit of projection by the warrior-oriented Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T06:29:49-07:00","id":1490020,"title":"","content":"It's probably worth mentioning that Gaian Garou don't have very optimal weapons for their Tier 4/5 fetishes. Labrys&lt;single edged axe , Mauls&lt;Warhammers, Klaives&lt;Conventionally shaped knives. This is probably because spirits would be happier housed in a grand and showy weapon rather than something more wieldy, convenient and practical. Though an extreme example, it's not wrong to move more in the direction of Frostmourne rather than Narsil. A level 5 Gnawer Fetish weapon would probably be more along the lines of a hand-crafted chainsword rather than something a weapons enthusiast would approve of. BSDS and most other direct agents of the Wyrm are extreme lunatics that don't care for their own lives or the concept of efficiency and would go even further in creating radical and depraved implements. For the most part, the supernatural physicality of the Garou lets them get away with less optimal weapon shapes like that of the Labrys or the Jarlhammer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type